<title>UK: Cobham unit bags Boeing defence order.</title>
<headline>Cobham unit bags Boeing defence order.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cobham Plc said on Tuesday that one of its subsidiaries Flight Refuelling Ltd had received orders from Boeing Space and Defence group valued at around 15 million dollars.</p>
<p>The order is for Flight Refuelling's Mk 32B air-to-air refuelling equipment.</p>
<p>The equipment would be used on Boeing's KC-135 strategic tanker which is currently in service with the United States Air Force and the French Air Force.</p>
<p>Cobham also said its U.S. unit Sargent Fletcher Inc bas acquired the aircraft external metal fuel tank business of Derlan Inc.</p>
<p>Sargent Fletcher paid four million dollars.</p>
<p>Derlan Inc is the wholly-owned U.S. subsidiary of Canada's Derlan Industries.</p>
